-- חוזר לבעלויות תשע"א/2: תשלום דמי הבראה ומענק יובל לשנת הלימודים תשע"א
-- The recuperation allowance (havraa) and the jubilee grant for school year
-- 2010/11: the day price, the days table, pro-rating by position and between
-- employers, the 140% limit, and who is owed the jubilee grant and how much.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `תשע"א/2 תשלום דמי הבראה ומענק יובל לשנת הלימודים תשע"א`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, title, date (1.6.2011), addressee and subject line; no rule.

-- Time is counted in school months of 2010/11 (common.l4: September 2010 =
-- 1, June 2011 = 10).

@desc A teaching employee's school year 2010/11 at one employer, as far as section 1 asks about it.
DECLARE `havraa year at an employer` HAS
    `years of teaching seniority`        IS A NUMBER @desc counted with the year being served (the first year is 1)
    `position at this employer`          IS A NUMBER @desc the share of a full position held at this employer that year (1 = one full position)
    `position at all employers`          IS A NUMBER @desc the share of a full position held at all employers together
    `months worked`                      IS A NUMBER @desc months of work in the school year

DECLARE `havraa action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the recuperation allowance` HAS `havraa paid` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the jubilee grant` HAS `grant paid` IS A NUMBER
    `work beyond 140% of a position`

§§ `1 קצובת דמי הבראה`

-- Section 1א: the allowance is paid in full with the June 2011 salary.
@ref akn:art_1__para_a
GIVEN h IS A `havraa year at an employer`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `havraa action`
DECIDE `paying the allowance with June's salary` h IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the recuperation allowance` `amount`
          PROVIDED `amount` AT LEAST `the recuperation allowance` h
    WITHIN `month number` June
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 1א: the allowance is paid in full with the June 2011 salary"

@export default The recuperation allowance one employer pays a teaching employee with the June 2011 salary under circular תשע"א/2
GIVEN h IS A `havraa year at an employer` @desc the employee's school year 2010/11 at this employer
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the recuperation allowance` h IS
    `recuperation days for year` (h's `years of teaching seniority`)
    TIMES `the recuperation-day price`
    TIMES `the havraa share at this employer` h

@ref akn:art_1__para_b
`the recuperation-day price` MEANS 411

-- Section 1ג's table as printed; it has no overlap and no hole from year 1.
@ref akn:art_1__para_c
DECLARE `havraa days band` HAS
    `from havraa year` IS A NUMBER
    `to havraa year`   IS A NUMBER @desc 999 stands for "ומעלה"
    `havraa band days` IS A NUMBER

`the table of recuperation days` MEANS
    LIST `havraa days band` 1  3   7,
         `havraa days band` 4  10  9,
         `havraa days band` 11 15  10,
         `havraa days band` 16 19  11,
         `havraa days band` 20 24  12,
         `havraa days band` 25 999 13

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `havraa days band`
DECIDE `the bands for year` n IS
    filter (GIVEN b YIELD n AT LEAST b's `from havraa year` AND n AT MOST b's `to havraa year`)
           `the table of recuperation days`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `recuperation days for year` n IS
    sum (map (GIVEN b YIELD b's `havraa band days`) (`the bands for year` n))

#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD count (`the bands for year` n) EQUALS 1)
            (LIST 1, 3, 4, 10, 11, 15, 16, 19, 20, 24, 25, 40)

-- Section 1ד: pro-rated to the part-time position "(1/10 for each month of
-- work)". F-2010-11_tashaa_02-a: a year has twelve months and the literal
-- tenths exceed the position. The reading adopted: the position share,
-- counted over at most ten months.
-- Section 1ה: at one employer, no more than one full position. Section 1ו:
-- where the positions at several employers total more than 100%, each
-- employer pays the share of the position held with it, so section 1ה's cap
-- is read per employer.
@ref akn:art_1__para_d akn:art_1__para_e akn:art_1__para_f
GIVEN h IS A `havraa year at an employer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the havraa share at this employer` h IS
    min (h's `position at this employer`) 1
    TIMES (min (h's `months worked`) 10 DIVIDED BY 10)

GIVEN h IS A `havraa year at an employer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the share by literal tenths` h IS
    min (h's `position at this employer`) 1
    TIMES (h's `months worked` DIVIDED BY 10)

-- Section 1ז: a teaching employee is restricted from working beyond 140% of a
-- position at all employers together, and section 1ו is no permission to
-- employ beyond it. The text sets no time limit.
@ref akn:art_1__para_g
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `havraa action`
DECIDE `the 140% limit` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    SHANT `work beyond 140% of a position`
    LEST BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1ז: no teaching employee works beyond 140% of a position at all employers together"

GIVEN h IS A `havraa year at an employer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within the 140% limit` h IF
    h's `position at all employers` AT MOST 1.4

§§ `2 תשלום מענק יובל`

@desc A teaching employee's record for the jubilee grant.
DECLARE `jubilee employee` HAS
    `teaching seniority set in September before the grant` IS A NUMBER @desc years of teaching at the employers, the owning bodies and formal education, military service included, as set in the September before the grant
    `teaching seniority on 1 June of the grant year`       IS A NUMBER @desc the same teaching seniority, military service included, completed on 1 June of the grant year
    `years of work in Israel on 1 June of the grant year`  IS A NUMBER @desc years of work in Israel completed on 1 June, compulsory IDF service included
    `unpaid-leave years with pension rights bought`        IS A NUMBER @desc years of unpaid leave for which pension rights were bought from the State or the teachers' pension funds
    `determining salary`                    IS A NUMBER @desc the salary determining pension and severance, without one-off yearly payments such as clothing and havraa; shekels
    `jubilee position fraction`             IS A NUMBER
    `share of the year employed`            IS A NUMBER @desc the fraction of the year the employee was employed

-- Section 2: the grant is paid with the June 2011 salary to those entitled:
-- 30 years and up of teaching seniority, military service included, as set
-- in the September of the year before the grant; 60% of the salary that
-- determines pension and severance, without one-off yearly payments.
@ref akn:art_2/p1
GIVEN j IS A `jubilee employee`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `havraa action`
DECIDE `paying the jubilee grant with June's salary` j IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the jubilee grant` `amount`
          PROVIDED `amount` AT LEAST `the jubilee grant` j
    WITHIN `month number` June
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 2: the jubilee grant is paid with the June 2011 salary"

GIVEN j IS A `jubilee employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the jubilee grant` j IS
    IF `entitled to the jubilee grant` j
    THEN j's `determining salary`
         TIMES 0.6
         TIMES `the jubilee share` j
    ELSE 0

GIVEN j IS A `jubilee employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the jubilee grant by section 2` j IF
    j's `teaching seniority set in September before the grant`
    PLUS j's `unpaid-leave years with pension rights bought`
    AT LEAST 30

-- akn:art_2/p2 The heading "הבהרות:" over the clarifications below; no rule.

-- Clarification א: a year of unpaid leave for which pension rights were bought
-- counts toward the years that entitle to the grant, by whichever measure
-- decides it (section 2 or clarification ב).
@ref akn:art_2__para_a
GIVEN j IS A `jubilee employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `unpaid leave counted toward the grant` j IS
    j's `unpaid-leave years with pension rights bought`

-- Clarification ב: 30 years of work in Israel completed on 1 June of the
-- year, compulsory IDF service included (F-2010-11_tashaa_02-b, -c).
@ref akn:art_2__para_b
GIVEN j IS A `jubilee employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the jubilee grant by clarification ב` j IF
    j's `years of work in Israel on 1 June of the grant year`
    PLUS `unpaid leave counted toward the grant` j
    AT LEAST 30

-- The reading adopted (F-2010-11_tashaa_02-b): clarification ב, the later
-- and more specific clause, decides the date, 1 June of the grant year.
-- (F-2010-11_tashaa_02-c): what is counted is section 2's own measure,
-- teaching seniority with military service (and clarification א's bought
-- years), completed by that date — as in every jubilee circular.
-- F-2010-11_tashaa_02-d: "30 שנה ומעלה" or once, in the year the 30 are
-- completed (clarification ב's "באותה שנה"). The reading adopted: once —
-- the years counted on 1 June within a year of 30 — as
-- F-2006-07_tashsaz_06-d and its siblings read the same words.
GIVEN j IS A `jubilee employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the jubilee grant` j IF
        `the years counted on 1 June` j AT LEAST 30
    AND `the years counted on 1 June` j LESS THAN 31

GIVEN j IS A `jubilee employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the years counted on 1 June` j IS
    j's `teaching seniority on 1 June of the grant year`
    PLUS `unpaid leave counted toward the grant` j

-- Section 2's own words, "30 שנה ומעלה", measured on 1 June, with no year
-- named.
@ref akn:art_2/p1
GIVEN j IS A `jubilee employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has the "30 years and more" section 2 names` j IF
    `the years counted on 1 June` j AT LEAST 30

-- Clarification ג: by the position fraction that year up to one position,
-- and by the share of the year employed.
@ref akn:art_2__para_c
GIVEN j IS A `jubilee employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the jubilee share` j IS
    min (j's `jubilee position fraction`) 1
    TIMES j's `share of the year employed`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off and signature; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

`a half-position teacher employed all twelve months` MEANS
    `havraa year at an employer` WITH
        `years of teaching seniority` IS 22
        `position at this employer`   IS 0.5
        `position at all employers`   IS 0.5
        `months worked`               IS 12

`the literal tenths give more than the position` MEANS
    `the share by literal tenths` `a half-position teacher employed all twelve months`
    GREATER THAN `a half-position teacher employed all twelve months`'s `position at this employer`
#ASSERT `the literal tenths give more than the position`

#ASSERT `the recuperation allowance` `a half-position teacher employed all twelve months` EQUALS 2466

`a teacher at two employers, 0.8 here` MEANS
    `havraa year at an employer` WITH
        `years of teaching seniority` IS 5
        `position at this employer`   IS 0.8
        `position at all employers`   IS 1.4
        `months worked`               IS 10

#ASSERT `the recuperation allowance` `a teacher at two employers, 0.8 here` EQUALS 2959.2
#ASSERT `within the 140% limit` `a teacher at two employers, 0.8 here`

`a teacher reaching 30 years between September and June` MEANS
    `jubilee employee` WITH
        `teaching seniority set in September before the grant` IS 29
        `teaching seniority on 1 June of the grant year`       IS 30
        `years of work in Israel on 1 June of the grant year`  IS 30
        `unpaid-leave years with pension rights bought`        IS 0
        `determining salary`                    IS 10000
        `jubilee position fraction`             IS 1
        `share of the year employed`            IS 1

`section 2 and clarification ב date the seniority differently` MEANS
    NOT (`entitled to the jubilee grant by section 2` `a teacher reaching 30 years between September and June`
         EQUALS `entitled to the jubilee grant by clarification ב` `a teacher reaching 30 years between September and June`)
#ASSERT `section 2 and clarification ב date the seniority differently`

`a teacher with ten years of other work in Israel` MEANS
    `jubilee employee` WITH
        `teaching seniority set in September before the grant` IS 20
        `teaching seniority on 1 June of the grant year`       IS 20
        `years of work in Israel on 1 June of the grant year`  IS 30
        `unpaid-leave years with pension rights bought`        IS 0
        `determining salary`                    IS 10000
        `jubilee position fraction`             IS 1
        `share of the year employed`            IS 1

`section 2 and clarification ב count different years` MEANS
        `entitled to the jubilee grant by clarification ב` `a teacher with ten years of other work in Israel`
    AND (NOT `entitled to the jubilee grant by section 2` `a teacher with ten years of other work in Israel`)
#ASSERT `section 2 and clarification ב count different years`
#ASSERT NOT `entitled to the jubilee grant` `a teacher with ten years of other work in Israel`

#ASSERT `the jubilee grant` `a teacher reaching 30 years between September and June` EQUALS 6000

-- Clarification א: a bought unpaid-leave year completes the thirty.
`a teacher with 29 years and one bought unpaid-leave year` MEANS
    `jubilee employee` WITH
        `teaching seniority set in September before the grant` IS 29
        `teaching seniority on 1 June of the grant year`       IS 29
        `years of work in Israel on 1 June of the grant year`  IS 29
        `unpaid-leave years with pension rights bought`        IS 1
        `determining salary`                    IS 10000
        `jubilee position fraction`             IS 0.5
        `share of the year employed`            IS 1
#ASSERT `the jubilee grant` `a teacher with 29 years and one bought unpaid-leave year` EQUALS 3000

#TRACE `paying the allowance with June's salary` `a half-position teacher employed all twelve months` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the recuperation allowance` 2466 AT 10
#TRACE `paying the jubilee grant with June's salary` `a teacher reaching 30 years between September and June` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the jubilee grant` 6000 AT 11
#TRACE `the 140% limit` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `work beyond 140% of a position` AT 3

§§ `Property checks`

-- The circular over its whole finite space: seniority years 1 to 60,
-- positions here and at all employers in tenths from 0 to 1.5, 0 to 12
-- months, and a career's years on 1 June from 0 to 45 in quarter years.

`tenths to 1.5` MEANS map (GIVEN k YIELD k DIVIDED BY 10) (range 0 15)

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, f IS A NUMBER, a IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `havraa year at an employer`
DECIDE `a checked year` n f a m IS
    `havraa year at an employer` WITH
        `years of teaching seniority` IS n
        `position at this employer`   IS f
        `position at all employers`   IS a
        `months worked`               IS m

-- 1ג: every year of seniority from 1 to 60 is in exactly one band, and the
-- days never fall.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD
                    count (`the bands for year` n) EQUALS 1
                AND `recuperation days for year` n AT MOST `recuperation days for year` (n PLUS 1))
            (range 1 60)

-- 1ד-1ו over every band edge, position here and month count: one employer
-- pays never less than nothing, never above 13 days at 411, never more for
-- a larger position or a month more, and the full allowance exactly for a
-- full position here and ten months; above a full position here it pays as
-- for one (1ה, at one employer). 1ה and 1ו never both apply: 1ה is for one
-- employer and 1ו for more than one, as their own words say. Within 1ז's
-- 140%, two employers together never pay more than 1.4 positions'.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD
                all (GIVEN f YIELD
                        all (GIVEN m YIELD
                                LET a MEANS `the recuperation allowance` (`a checked year` n f f m)
                                    full MEANS `recuperation days for year` n TIMES `the recuperation-day price`
                                IN      a AT LEAST 0
                                    AND a AT MOST 13 TIMES `the recuperation-day price`
                                    AND a AT MOST `the recuperation allowance` (`a checked year` n (f PLUS 0.1) (f PLUS 0.1) m)
                                    AND a AT MOST `the recuperation allowance` (`a checked year` n f f (m PLUS 1))
                                    AND (a EQUALS full) EQUALS (f AT LEAST 1 AND m AT LEAST 10))
                            (range 0 12))
                    `tenths to 1.5`)
            (LIST 1, 3, 4, 10, 11, 15, 16, 19, 20, 24, 25, 60)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN f YIELD
                all (GIVEN g YIELD
                        LET h1 MEANS `a checked year` 12 f (f PLUS g) 10
                            h2 MEANS `a checked year` 12 g (f PLUS g) 10
                        IN  (NOT `within the 140% limit` h1)
                            OR `the recuperation allowance` h1 PLUS `the recuperation allowance` h2
                               AT MOST 1.4 TIMES `recuperation days for year` 12 TIMES `the recuperation-day price`)
                    `tenths to 1.5`)
            `tenths to 1.5`

-- Section 2 on the readings adopted, over a career's years on 1 June from
-- 0 to 45 in quarter years: the grant falls in the year the 30 are
-- completed and no other, never above 60% of the determining salary.
GIVEN t IS A NUMBER, f IS A NUMBER, s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `jubilee employee`
DECIDE `a checked jubilee employee` t f s IS
    `jubilee employee` WITH
        `teaching seniority set in September before the grant` IS t MINUS 0.75
        `teaching seniority on 1 June of the grant year`       IS t
        `years of work in Israel on 1 June of the grant year`  IS t
        `unpaid-leave years with pension rights bought`        IS 0
        `determining salary`                    IS 10000
        `jubilee position fraction`             IS f
        `share of the year employed`            IS s

#ASSERT all (GIVEN q YIELD
                `entitled to the jubilee grant` (`a checked jubilee employee` (q DIVIDED BY 4) 1 1)
                EQUALS (q AT LEAST 120 AND q LESS THAN 124))
            (range 0 180)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN f YIELD
                all (GIVEN s YIELD
                        LET g MEANS `the jubilee grant` (`a checked jubilee employee` 30 f s)
                        IN      g AT LEAST 0
                            AND g AT MOST 6000
                            AND g AT MOST `the jubilee grant` (`a checked jubilee employee` 30 (f PLUS 0.1) s)
                            AND g AT MOST `the jubilee grant` (`a checked jubilee employee` 30 f (s PLUS 0.25)))
                    (LIST 0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1))
            `tenths to 1.5`

-- F-2010-11_tashaa_02-d: over the same career, section 2's "30 שנה ומעלה"
-- and the once-only reading part in exactly the years from the 31st on; a
-- teacher in year 35 is in the one and not the other.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN q YIELD
                (NOT (`has the "30 years and more" section 2 names` (`a checked jubilee employee` (q DIVIDED BY 4) 1 1)
                      EQUALS `entitled to the jubilee grant` (`a checked jubilee employee` (q DIVIDED BY 4) 1 1)))
                EQUALS (q AT LEAST 124))
            (range 0 180)

`"30 years and more" reaches a 35-year teacher, the once-only reading does not` MEANS
        `has the "30 years and more" section 2 names` (`a checked jubilee employee` 35 1 1)
    AND NOT `entitled to the jubilee grant` (`a checked jubilee employee` 35 1 1)
#ASSERT `"30 years and more" reaches a 35-year teacher, the once-only reading does not`
